{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04HG", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nV \\ar[r] \\ar[dr] & X_U \\ar[d] \\ar[r] & X \\ar[d]^f \\\\\n& U \\ar[r] & S\n}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-morphisms-section-etale-localization}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{more-morphisms-equation-basic-diagram}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ab88dd81a7557aa89abd9877b8b94af4f133290c5b400393b55ce00f95aca86b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a103889523313a974080e6fc78fbd0b44107073f401c593aaca847ed0ac6881f", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the chapter\nMore on Morphisms, Section <REF_0001>\nthe reader can find some results on the <ACCENT_0001>tale local structure of\nquasi-finite morphisms. In this section we want to combine this\nwith the topological properties of unramified morphisms we have seen\nin this chapter. The basic overall picture to keep in mind is\n<MATH_0001>\nsee\nMore on Morphisms, Equation (<REF_0002>).\nWe start with a very general case.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:15a2a8edc8741221656c6106931687afd7d2d67f424c2f3c1a10c05cabf3c480", "unit_id": "tag:04HG:prose-0001"}
